g Expenses","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"oi":{"c":"us-gaap:OperatingIncomeLoss","l":"Total segment operating income (loss)","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"pretax":{"c":"us-gaap:IncomeLossFromContinuingOperationsBeforeIncomeTaxesExtraordinaryItemsNoncontrollingInterest","l":"Income (Loss) from Continuing Operations before Income Taxes, Noncontrolling Interest","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ni":{"c":"us-gaap:NetIncomeLoss","l":"Net income (loss)","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ocf":{"c":"us-gaap:NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities","l":"Cash Provided by (Used in) Operating Activity, Including Discontinued Operation","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"da":{"c":"us-gaap:DepreciationAndAmortization","l":"Depreciation, Depletion and Amortization, Nonproduction","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"sbc":{"c":"us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensation","l":"Share-based Payment Arrangement, Noncash Expense","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"}},"co_fcf":null,"co_status":"not_reported","co_errors":0,"co_tried":1},"2026-06-30":{"end":"2026-06-30","label":"Q2 2026","fq":2,"fy":2026,"cal":"CY2026Q2","form":"10-Q","accn":"0001493152-26-035909","filed":"2026-08-04","doc_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1535955/000149315226035909/form10-q.htm","index_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1535955/000149315226035909/0001493152-26-035909-index.htm","raw":{"revenue":190099,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":2041389,"sm":null,"ga":990956,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":3032345,"oi":-2842246,"pretax":-2622395,"tax":200,"ni":-2622595,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-3028427,"da":14648,"dep":null,"amort":null,"sbc":58145,"rev_contract":null,"capex":null},"q1_end":"2026-03-31","py_end":"2025-06-30","raw_q1":{"revenue":119397,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":2764394,"sm":null,"ga":1204467,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":3968861,"oi":-3849464,"pretax":-3671894,"tax":null,"ni":-3671894,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-2257137,"da":14814,"dep":null,"amort":null,"sbc":65398,"rev_contract":null,"capex":null},"raw_py":{"revenue":622849,"cor":null,"gp":null,"rd":2136769,"sm":null,"ga":890433,"sga":null,"costs_total":null,"opex_total":3027202,"oi":-2404353,"pretax":-2205716,"tax":0,"ni":-2205716,"pl":null,"nci":null,"ocf":-1886234,"da":16108,"dep":null,"amort":null,"sbc":65205,"rev_contract":null,"capex":null},"lines_struct":null,"lines":null,"lines_py":null,"notes":{"rd":[{"heading":"Research and Development Expenses","text":"Research and development expenses consist primarily of salaries, benefits, stock-based compensation and related personnel costs, fees paid to external service providers such as contract research organizations and contract manufacturing organizations, contractual obligations for clinical development, clinical sites, manufacturing and scale-up for late stage clinical trials, formulation of clinical drug supplies, and expenses associated with regulatory submissions. Research and development expenses also include an allocation of indirect costs, such as those for facilities, office expense, and depreciation of equipment based on the ratio of direct labor hours for research and development personnel to total direct labor hours for all personnel. We expense research and development expenses as incurred."}],"ga":[{"heading":"General and Administrative Expenses","text":"General and administrative expenses consist primarily of salaries and related benefits, including stock-based compensation, and outside consulting services related to our executive, finance, business development and administrative support functions. Other general and administrative expenses include rent and utilities, travel expenses, and professional fees for auditing, tax, legal, and various other services.\n\nGeneral and administrative expenses also include expenses for the cost of preparing, filing and prosecuting patent applications and maintaining, enforcing and defending intellectual property-related claims.\n\nWe expect that general and administrative expenses will increase in the future as we continue as a public company. These fees include legal and consulting fees, accounting and audit fees, director fees, directors\u2019 and officers\u2019 insurance premiums, fees for investor relations services and enhanced business and accounting systems, litigation costs, professional fees and other costs. However, if we are unable to raise additional capital, we may need to reduce general and administrative expenses in order to extend our ability to continue as a going concern."}],"nonop":[{"heading":"Other Income and Expense","text":"Other income and expense consists primarily of interest income earned on our cash, cash equivalents and marketable investment securities."}],"ocf":[{"heading":"Net Cash from Operating Activities","text":"During the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, net cash used in operating activities was $5.3 million and $3.9 million, respectively.\n\nNet cash used in operating activities during the six months ended June 30, 2026, was primarily attributable to cash required to support our LPCN 1154 clinical trial activities and our ongoing operations. Net cash used in operating activities during the six months ended June 30, 2025, was primarily attributable to cash required to support ongoing operations."}],"sbc":[{"heading":null,"text":"Research and development expenses consist primarily of salaries, benefits, stock-based compensation and related personnel costs, fees paid to external service providers such as contract research organizations and contract manufacturing organizations, contractual obligations for clinical development, clinical sites, manufacturing and scale-up for late stage clinical trials, formulation of clinical drug supplies, and expenses associated with regulatory submissions. Research and development expenses also include an allocation of indirect costs, such as those for facilities, office expense, and depreciation of equipment based on the ratio of direct labor hours for research and development personnel to total direct labor hours for all personnel. We expense research and development expenses as incurred. Since our inception, we have spent approximately $168.0 million in research and development expenses through June 30, 2026."}],"net sales":[{"heading":"Revenue","text":"To date, we have not generated any revenues from product sales and do not expect to do so until our FDA approved product receives regulatory approval outside the U.S. and Canada or until one of our product candidates receives approval from the FDA. Revenues to date have been generated substantially from license fees, royalty and milestone payments and research support from our licensees. Since our inception through June 30, 2026, we have generated $55.4 million in revenue under our various license and collaboration arrangements and from government grants. We have entered into the Verity License Agreement, the SPC License Agreement, the Pharmalink Distribution Agreement and the Ach\u00e9 License Agreement with the potential for revenue from future milestones, royalties and/or product sales, but we may never generate revenues from any of our clinical or preclinical development programs or licensed products as we may never succeed in obtaining regulatory approval or commercializing any of these product candidates."}]},"capex_src":null,"src":{"revenue":{"c":"us-gaap:Revenues","l":"Revenues","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"rd":{"c":"us-gaap:ResearchAndDevelopmentExpense","l":"Research and development","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"ga":{"c":"us-gaap:GeneralAndAdministrativeExpense","l":"General and administrative","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"opex_total":{"c":"us-gaap:OperatingExpenses","l":"Operating Expenses","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"oi":{"c":"us-gaap:OperatingIncomeLoss","l":"Total segment operating income (loss)","ytd":false,"how":"xbrl"},"pretax":{"c":"us-gaap:IncomeLossFromContinuingOperationsBeforeIncomeTaxesExtraordinaryItemsNoncontrollingInterest","l":"Income (Loss) from Continuing Operations before Income Taxes, Noncont